==========================================================================================
 CAP RECONSTRUCTION via the magic function (inclusion-exclusion), checking the order where it BREAKS
==========================================================================================
  j   P (minimizer) order-1 (union)  order-2 (pairwise)       order-3    full=cap   known cap
  2         (1, 13)          0.7143             0.72527       0.72527     0.72527     0.72527
      -> order-2 (pairwise magic function) is EXACT: 66/91 = cap  [CYCLOTOMIC, f-hat>=0 Fejer]
  3     (1, 12, 13)          0.5714             0.61538       0.60440     0.60440     0.60440
  4 (1, 11, 12, 13)          0.4286             0.52814       0.48327     0.49426     0.49426
      -> order-2 gives 0.52814; the ORDER-3 correction = -37/1092 = the binding deviation constant
  5 (1, 5, 7, 8, 9)          0.2857             0.48520       0.31599     0.38146     0.38146
      -> order-2 gives 0.48520; the ORDER-3 correction = -61/588 = the binding deviation constant
==========================================================================================
 MAGIC FUNCTION = order-2 pairwise overlap kernel (exact cap for j<=3) + order-3 correction (j=4,5).
 The kernel K(p,q) is cyclotomic (min at antipode q=-1 mod14); the order-3 = the two hard constants.
